                  <provenance type="#m"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_95">Cambridge,
                        Cambridgeshire. Dominican convent</orgName><p>Notes signed by John
                        Crafford (friar of the Cambridge convent in 1411 and 1412; BRUC 165) on
                        fols. 135, 136, 184 (same hand as Vat. lat. 7095 and Ottob. lat. 187) and
                        one by him on fol. 184r beginning 'Nota bene passum quia yngham. . .' (?John
                        de Yngham, Clare Hall fellow 1402; BRUC 326).</p><p>'rokell' is against a
                        note on fol. 135r and 'Rokell' is in margins of fols. 149r, 259r (?John
                        Rokyll, prior-provincial before 1427; BRUO 2210--11).</p><p>'Caucio
                        \fratris/ Iohannis fe.r.y exposita cist' de [. . .]' (fol.
                        334v).</p><p>Bound with a 15th-cent. copy of Aquinas's Quodlibeta, in an
                        English hand.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Marcello Cervini (1501--1555), cardinal, his
                     no. 51.</provenance>
